      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Exception Safety and Resource Leaks in `openDevice`**\n\n* **Issue:** In `IapControl::openDevice`, you manually manage the `handle` before wrapping it in the smart pointer:\n\n```c\nlibusb_device_handle *handle \u003d nullptr;\nif (libusb_open(found_dev, \u0026handle) !\u003d 0) { ... }\nfor (...) {\n    if (libusb_claim_interface(...) !\u003d 0) {\n        libusb_close(handle); // Manual cleanup\n        return -1;\n    }\n}\nm_devHandlePtr.reset(handle);\n```\n\n  If `libusb_detach_kernel_driver` or something else were to throw an exception or fail unexpectedly, the handle could leak.\n\n\n* **Remediation:** Pass ownership to your `unique_ptr` immediately after a successful open.\n\n```c\nlibusb_device_handle *handle \u003d nullptr;\nif (libusb_open(found_dev, \u0026handle) !\u003d 0) { ... return -1; }\nm_devHandlePtr.reset(handle); // Safely managed now\n\nfor (size_t i \u003d 0; i \u003c m_hidInterfaces.size(); i++) {\n    // use m_devHandlePtr.get() for operations\n    // No manual libusb_close() needed on failure!\n}\n```",
