      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Inconsistent Output Buffers (`std::cout` vs `stdout`)**\n\n* **Issue:** In `utility.h`, `logInfo` writes to `std::cout`. However, in `iaptool.cc` `setProgressBar`, you explicitly call `fflush(stdout)`. Mixing C++ streams and C standard I/O streams can lead to interleaved or poorly synchronized console output.  \n* **Remediation:** Stick to the C++ streams. To flush `std::cout`, use `std::flush`:\n\n```c\nlogInfo(\" {} % [Data {} of {}]\", percent, progress, totalSize);\nstd::cout \u003c\u003c std::flush;\n```",
